cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Cross-scale organization of the atmospheric circulation: a falsification-grade research program (Shroedinger, gen3)"
version: "4.0"
type: software
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Theclimateguy/Shroedinger"
url: "https://github.com/Theclimateguy/Shroedinger"
date-released: 2026-08-14
authors:
  - family-names: "Sotiriadi"
    given-names: "N."
abstract: >-
  Code, frozen protocols and results of a preregistered research program on
  the cross-scale organization of the atmospheric circulation, computed from
  ERA5 and MERRA-2 reanalyses. Two descriptors of the 850 hPa relative
  vorticity field are introduced and tested: the cross-scale envelope-coupling
  profile P (spatial rank correlation of activity maps of adjacent octave
  levels) and the transfer-asymmetry index A (norm of the commutator of the
  estimated aggregation and detailing operators). Both form stable regional
  signatures across seasons, years and ENSO phases; the index A additionally
  carries information beyond the power spectrum, beyond P and beyond
  semi-fractal level characteristics, and its regional geography replicates
  across reanalyses (ERA5 vs MERRA-2, Spearman rho = 0.93). The release
  contains eight frozen protocols with deviation logs, an independent
  methodological audit and its remediation, a full catalogue of the program's
  negative results, per-region-window numerical results and figures, and a
  table of all 73 experiments across three generations of the program.
keywords:
  - hierarchical organization of geosystems
  - scale invariants
  - atmospheric circulation
  - cross-scale coupling
  - ERA5
  - MERRA-2
  - reanalysis
  - reproducible research
